---
import PhaseLayout from '../../layouts/PhaseLayout.astro';
---

<PhaseLayout title="Richard Feynman — Polymath.Sys" activeNav="polymaths">

<style>
  .pm-back { display:inline-block; font-family:monospace; font-size:11px; color:#888; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:2rem; letter-spacing:0.05em; }
  .pm-back:hover { color:#111; }
  .polymath-single { max-width:860px; }
  .pm-header { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1.5rem; margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
  .pm-initials { width:64px; height:64px; border-radius:50%; background:#111; color:#fff; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-family:monospace; font-size:18px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.1em; flex-shrink:0; }
  .pm-name { font-size:22px; font-weight:700; color:#111; letter-spacing:-0.02em; }
  .pm-years { font-family:monospace; font-size:12px; color:#888; margin-top:4px; }
  .pm-bio { font-size:14px; line-height:1.8; color:#444; margin-bottom:1.5rem; padding:1.2rem 1.5rem; border-left:3px solid #222; background:#fafafa; }
  .pm-domains { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0.5rem; margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
  .pm-contributions { margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
  .pm-section-title { font-family:monospace; font-size:10px; letter-spacing:0.15em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#888; margin-bottom:0.8rem; }
  .pm-contributions ul { padding-left:1.5rem; }
  .pm-contributions li { font-size:13px; color:#444; line-height:1.7; margin-bottom:0.4rem; }
  .pm-quote { margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
  .pm-quote blockquote { font-size:13px; color:#555; line-height:1.8; border-left:2px solid #ccc; padding-left:1rem; margin:0; font-style:italic; }
  .pm-reading { margin-bottom:2rem; }
  .pm-reading ul { padding-left:1.5rem; }
  .pm-reading li { font-size:13px; color:#444; line-height:1.7; margin-bottom:0.4rem; }
  .pm-era { display:inline-block; font-family:monospace; font-size:10px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; padding:0.3rem 0.8rem; border:1px solid #ccc; color:#888; margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
</style>

  <a href="/polymaths" class="pm-back">&larr; Hall of Legends</a>

  <div class="polymath-single">

    <div class="pm-era">Modern · 1918–1988</div>

    <div class="pm-header">
      <div class="pm-initials">RF</div>
      <div>
        <div class="pm-name">Richard Feynman</div>
        <div class="pm-years">1918--1988</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-bio">Nobel laureate, safecracker, bongo player, artist, and the greatest physics teacher who ever lived. Feynman revolutionized quantum electrodynamics with his Feynman diagrams, worked on the Manhattan Project at Los Alamos, cracked the cause of the Challenger disaster, pioneered quantum computing, and taught generations of physicists through his legendary Caltech lectures. He embodied the joy of finding things out.</div>

    <div class="pm-domains">
      <span class="rtag free">Physics</span>
      <span class="rtag must">Mathematics</span>
      <span class="rtag vid">Teaching</span>
      <span class="rtag book">Computing</span>
      <span class="rtag free">Biology</span>
      <span class="rtag must">Art</span>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-contributions">
      <div class="pm-section-title">Greatest Contributions</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Developed Feynman diagrams for visualizing quantum interactions, revolutionizing particle physics</li>
        <li>Reformulated quantum mechanics via the path integral formulation</li>
        <li>Proposed quantum computing (1982), launching the field decades before practical quantum computers</li>
        <li>Created the <em>Feynman Lectures on Physics</em>, the gold standard of physics education</li>
        <li>Identified the O-ring failure that caused the Challenger disaster through a simple ice-water demonstration</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-quote">
      <div class="pm-section-title">Key Insight</div>
      <blockquote>"What I cannot create, I do not understand." -- Feynman's method: rebuild every concept from first principles. If you can't explain it simply, you don't understand it deeply enough. His "Feynman Technique" for learning remains the gold standard.</blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-reading">
      <div class="pm-section-title">Recommended Reading</div>
      <ul>
        <li><em>"Surely You're Joking, Mr. Feynman!"</em> -- Richard Feynman (1985)</li>
        <li><em>The Feynman Lectures on Physics</em> -- Richard Feynman, Robert Leighton, Matthew Sands</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>

</PhaseLayout>
